[
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `rewrite` fails.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Extensionality works.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">-- exact Eq.symm (funext h)</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In the above code <code>rw</code> fails with the following error message:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>Tactic `rewrite` failed: Did not find an occurrence of the pattern\n  f ?x\nin the target expression\n  (fun n =&gt; g n) = fun n =&gt; f n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Is this expected behaviour of the <code>rewrite</code> tactic? I would have expected the <code>?x</code> metavariable to capture <code>n</code> in <code>f n</code> and replace <code>f n</code> to <code>g n</code></p>\n<hr>\n<p>Ultimately, I have an use case which looks like the following snippet, but  where extensionality is somewhat tricky to prove... Having something like <code>rw</code> would be very useful there.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Q</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 593173269,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1778050530
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, this is expected. In general <code>rw</code> does not work under binders. Note that <code>fun n =&gt; g n</code> is definitionally equal to <code>g</code>, so you are really proving <code>g = f</code>, that is exactly the statement of of <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=funext#doc\">docs#funext</a> (except for the order) that is basically an axiom in Lean's type theory.</p>",
        "id": 593174825,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1778051021
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As far as I know, <code>rw</code> expects \"bare\" equalities or equivalences.</p>\n<p>So either use <code>funext</code> as you suggest</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">funext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or change your assumption</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 593174831,
        "sender_full_name": "fiforeach",
        "timestamp": 1778051024
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"130384\">@Riccardo Brasca</span> , <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1006462\">@fiforeach</span>  Thank you very much!</p>\n<p>My particular use case looks more like the following, but <code>P</code> is a long expression which I can't manually just put in the code, and is not getting inferred if I try putting a hole in its place</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Eq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">funext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">congrArg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<hr>\n<p>To try giving some more context about the condition I am in right now, this is what the <code>rw</code> error looks like for me:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>Tactic `rewrite` failed: Did not find an occurrence of the pattern\n  @CT.Func.Mor.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G ?m.29 ?m.29 (@CT.Category.id.{0, 0} 𝓧 ?m.29)\nin the target expression\n  @Eq.{1} (CT.Func.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑)) G\n    (@CT.Func.mk.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑)\n      (fun (x : CT.Category.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓧) =&gt;\n        @CT.Func.mk.{0, 0} 𝓐 𝓑\n          (fun (a : CT.Category.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓐) =&gt;\n            @CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓐 𝓑 (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G x) a)\n          (fun {X Y : CT.Category.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓐} (f : CT.Category.Hom.{0, 0} 𝓐 X Y) =&gt;\n            @CT.Category.seq.{0, 0} 𝓑 (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓐 𝓑 (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G x) X)\n              (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓐 𝓑 (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G x) Y)\n              (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓐 𝓑 (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G x) Y)\n              (@CT.Func.Mor.{0, 0} 𝓐 𝓑 (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G x) X Y f)\n              (@CT.NatTransform.component.{0, 0} 𝓐 𝓑 (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G x)\n                (@CT.Func.Obj.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G x)\n                (@CT.Func.Mor.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G x x (@CT.Category.id.{0, 0} 𝓧 x)) Y))\n          (@C.Cat.exp.curry._proof_2.{0} 𝓐 𝓑 𝓧\n            (@C.seq.{0} (@CT.Product.obj.{1, 0} C.Cat.{0} 𝓧 𝓐 (C.Cat.prod.{0} 𝓧 𝓐))\n              (@CT.Product.obj.{1, 0} C.Cat.{0} (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) 𝓐 (C.Cat.prod.{0} (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) 𝓐)) 𝓑 ...\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The pattern does appear in the form of <code>@CT.Func.Mor.{0, 0} 𝓧 (C.Cat.exp.obj.{0} 𝓐 𝓑) G x x (@CT.Category.id.{0, 0} 𝓧 x)</code>, but <code>?m.29</code> is not being inferred as <code>x</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<p>All suggestions are welcome, also I would try to produce a better MWE for my problem</p>",
        "id": 593176966,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1778051788
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>rw</code> will not work under a <code>fun</code>, there is no way around it. Have you tried <code>simp_rw</code>?</p>",
        "id": 593177367,
        "sender_full_name": "Riccardo Brasca",
        "timestamp": 1778051911
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1006462\">fiforeach</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/.60rw.60.20tactic.20failure/near/593174831\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As far as I know, <code>rw</code> expects \"bare\" equalities or equivalences.</p>\n<p>So either use <code>funext</code> as you suggest</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">funext</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or change your assumption</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Although your suggestions are on point, it is not the case that <code>rw</code> only accepts \"bare equalities\". It also accepts equalities with a variable in them such as the <code>h</code> in the mwe or <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=mul_comm#doc\">docs#mul_comm</a>, and even equalities which only hold under some condition like <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ENat.coe_toNat#doc\">docs#ENat.coe_toNat</a>, in which case it will create a separate goal to prove that the appropriate condition holds.</p>",
        "id": 593177443,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1778051934
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Putting it a somewhat less verbosely, the error I am getting is</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Text only\"><pre><span></span><code>Tactic `rewrite` failed: Did not find an occurrence of the pattern\n  G.Mor 𝓧.id\nin the target expression\n  G =\n    {\n      Obj := fun x =&gt;\n        { Obj := fun a =&gt; (G.Obj x).Obj a, Mor := fun {X Y} f =&gt; 𝓑.seq ((G.Obj x).Mor f) ((G.Mor 𝓧.id).component Y),\n          proof_id := ⋯, proof_comp := ⋯ },\n      Mor := fun {X Y} f =&gt; { component := fun x =&gt; 𝓑.seq ((G.Obj X).Mor 𝓐.id) ((G.Mor f).component x), proof := ⋯ },\n      proof_id := ⋯, proof_comp := ⋯ }\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>where <code>G.Mor 𝓧.id</code> is actually <code>@Func.Mor 𝓧 (obj 𝓐 𝓑) G ?x ?x 𝓧.id</code></p>\n<hr>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"130384\">@Riccardo Brasca</span> I was not using mathlib, let me try importing it and using <code>simp_rw</code></p>",
        "id": 593178089,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1778052145
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"130384\">@Riccardo Brasca</span> I tried using <code>simp_rw</code> after importing <code>Mathlib.Tactic.SimpRw</code>. This does not work.</p>\n<p>I really need to think and make a better MWE for this issue...</p>",
        "id": 593179599,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1778052603
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>some thoughts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>based on the names and patterns of snippet, you appear to be proving an equality of what seem to effectively be functors. This can be justified in some cases, but generally equality of functors is \"evil\" and one should consider proving natural isomorphism instead.</li>\n<li>You are in a situation where you want to prove values of some <code>structure</code> equal, where one side is a variable. In my experience, this is a situation where you'd like to use an <code>ext</code>-lemma, saying two terms of a structure-type are equal when they agree on their fields. Alternatively, you can immediately use <code>cases</code> on the variable (in this case <code>G</code>) to directly compare fields.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 593199131,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1778058059
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Functor.ext#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Functor.ext</a> for what an extentionality lemma for functors can look like, in particular the casting using <code>eqTohom</code> to make things typecheck</p>",
        "id": 593199496,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1778058138
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"684366\">@Edward van de Meent</span> </p>\n<ul>\n<li>Yes, I am indeed trying to show equality of functors. <a href=\"https://github.com/Ryan-Hota/catThy/blob/main/CatStruct_Attempt2.lean\">This</a> is the project that I am currently working on; we are trying to prove (from scratch) that the category of categories is cartesian closed. The equality requirement of functors is because we have defined exponential objects (<code>CategoryTheory.Exponential</code>) in that way (see the <code>proof_exists</code> and <code>proof_unique</code> fields). I am not entirely sure now if that was the right decision, or if we should switch to isomorphism instead of equality.</li>\n<li>I have tried a lot to work it out by using <code>ext</code>, but the issue I keep hitting is that the type of <code>Func.Mor</code> is dependent on the type of <code>Func.Obj</code>. When the types of <code>Func.Mor</code> of two differenty functors are definitionally equivalent, then I can get away with <code>ext</code> (for example, in <code>Cat.exp.proof_exists</code>); but if they are only propositionally equal then I keep getting <code>HEq</code> goals, which reduce to showing <code>cast</code> equalities (for example, <code>Cat.exp.proof_unique</code>). That is the main reason why I wanted to start anew and focus on rewriting and simplifying the expressions (using <code>rw</code> or something) before attempting <code>ext</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 593205694,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1778059593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"684366\">Edward van de Meent</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/.60rw.60.20tactic.20failure/near/593199496\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.Functor.ext#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.Functor.ext</a> for what an extentionality lemma for functors can look like, in particular the casting using <code>eqTohom</code> to make things typecheck</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Thank you very much, let me see if I can get any new ideas from here and solve my issue.</p>",
        "id": 593205984,
        "sender_full_name": "Soham Saha",
        "timestamp": 1778059660
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Apt wording in the description for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/EqToHom.html#CategoryTheory.eqToHom\">eqToHom</a></p>\n<p>\"Dependent type theory hell\" nicely sums up what I have been doing for the past two days...</p>",
